{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361396,"nonce":"Bgl+Bc0BYv2nAf5Q0FHr5q9zN4M=","title":"with takes one handler and no constructor arguments","message":"`with_stmt` in crates/zynml/ml.zyn parses `with NAME { body }` only. The typed AST already carries a list with arguments (`TypedWith::handlers: Vec\u003cTypedWithHandler\u003e`, each with `args`), but `TypedCfgBuilder` records only the first handler as a `WithScopeInfo` and nothing reads `args`. Nesting `with A { with B { } }` covers several handlers today. There is no way to initialize handler state from the scope (`with Pool(capacity = 4096) { }`), so every state field starts from its declared initializer in `H$new`.\n\nDone: `with A, B { }` pushes the handlers in order and pops them in reverse on every exit edge. `with H(args) { }` passes the arguments to the state constructor, which takes them in place of the corresponding field initializers; a handler without state refuses arguments with a diagnostic.","files":null}]}